# Dragon Quest VII Reimagined (PPSA17942) — title -> new adventure log -> name entry ->
# first-run System Settings -> opening chapter -> FREE FIELD CONTROL in Pilchard Bay.
#
# THIS IS THE ROUTE THAT PRODUCED THE EVIDENCE, byte-for-byte. Do not extend it without re-running:
# a published recipe that has never been executed is worth nothing.
#
# What it changes against reach-gameplay.pad is how much confirm the opening chapter is given.
# That route advances dialogue every 15 s and stops at t=700; this one presses every 2 s to
# t=1180. Measured on one binary, quiet box, world phase only, classifying by the field HUD
# (minimap + party block, with a structure floor so a flat colour collapse cannot pass):
#
#     route                    confirms   frames with the field HUD
#     reach-gameplay.pad         41         0
#     a probe route (see #1874)  37         0
#     THIS ROUTE                447       144    (t=652..1240 s, 588 s)
#
# It delivers only Cross, so it establishes the FIELD STATE, not locomotion.
#
# The two comparison routes also stop earlier than this one, so spacing is not the only
# difference between them — but it is the one that matters, because every screen in the chapter
# waits indefinitely for confirm. A press that lands early is absorbed, not lost, which is also
# why this route tolerates the wall-clock drift of #2764.
#
# Read scripts/dragon-quest-vii/README.md for the control model before editing above 320 s —
# OPTIONS is the jump-to-OK shortcut on the name keyboard, and the two System Settings menus
# have DIFFERENT row counts.

